    "created_at": "2023-05-27T07:36:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-27T07:36:00Z",
    "body": "Ah, great, Chrome and Firefox don't agree. Chrome's special case uses the document's base URL, Firefox's special case uses the document's URL. (And Safari, at least by code inspection, doesn't have a special case.)\r\n\r\nThis does give us a bit more freedom to try to align on Safari's behavior, which is the simplest. But Safari's behavior feels more likely to break sites to me. In 99% of cases, there is no base URL, so Chrome and Firefox have the same observable behavior. And at least one web developer (in https://github.com/jsdom/jsdom/issues/3513) was expecting that Chrome/Firefox behavior. So we should probably still pick one of them.\r\n\r\nDoes anyone have strong opinions on which? @smaug---- @natechapin",
