    "created_at": "2023-05-27T16:03:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-27T16:11:13Z",
    "body": "It appears ancient — predates Blink, was present when WebKit first landed History in 2009:\r\n\r\n![lines from ancient commit with if (urlString.isEmpty()) case](https://github.com/whatwg/html/assets/6257356/114b023b-aa2c-40a5-8517-7450037a3c6b)\r\n\r\nAt the time that was committed, [this was what the tentative spec looked like](https://web.archive.org/web/20091203015337/http://www.whatwg.org/specs/web-apps/current-work/multipage/history.html#dom-history-pushstate). I don’t see anything there about the empty string, but the URL resolving/parsing algorithm was very different then — and it looks like the empty string [would have thrown](https://web.archive.org/web/20091006214949/http://www.w3.org/html/wg/href/draft#parse-a-url) if passed to the resolution algorithm as RFC 3986’s `URI-reference` (which it delegated to) doesn’t include the empty string. That might explain why it was special-cased in the implementation despite the spec not saying to do so! (Of course, I’m scanning these old spec texts in mental sloppy mode and might be missing something.)\r\n\r\nThat info probably isn’t useful (I was just curious to try figuring it out), but knowing it dates back to 2009 might be useful, since I think 14 years of empty string special casing strengthens the case for specifying the WebKit/Blink behavior.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
