    "created_at": "2023-05-31T14:11:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-31T14:11:17Z",
    "body": "> urlForState is not what [pushState/replaceState call](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/e8c12535c74ae70cd22109daed317e6fe4df2f73/Source/WebCore/page/History.h#L95-L103) as far as I can tell. They call [stateObjectAdded](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/e8c12535c74ae70cd22109daed317e6fe4df2f73/Source/WebCore/page/History.cpp#L186-L287) [...]\r\n\r\nMy mention of it may have been misleading, sorry: that was “archaeological”. I was trying to determine where it first appeared, and in 2009 when Webkit introduced pushState and replaceState, `urlForState` was (afaict) where URL argument resolution happened (`JSHistory::pushState` → `History::stateObjectAdded` → `History::urlForState`) and the special casing of the empty string was already present. In current Webkit, it looks very different.",
